WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Mutation-guided generation
starts from a fault concern.

00:00:02.766 --> 00:00:07.360
Select a meaningful change,
generate a candidate test, and preserve

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.960
the intended assertion.
The candidate must pass the original

00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:14.480
implementation and fail the faulty
variant for the intended reason.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:19.040
Exclude invalid or equivalent
mutations before judging the result.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.160
Retain the fault rationale
with the run evidence.

00:00:22.263 --> 00:00:24.960
Detecting selected mutations
improves the challenge

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.080
but does not prove that
every real defect is covered.
